    "chunk_text": "Enfection\u2019s AI Marketing Playbook lands in Australia\n\nEnfection, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading marketing technology company, has officially set up operations in Melbourne, Australia, marking a significant milestone in its regional expansion strategy and reinforcing its ambition to become a category leader in AI powered marketing transformation across the Asia Pacific region.\n\nAs part of this expansion, the company has been conducting a series of workshops in Melbourne designed to train business leaders and entrepreneurs on the latest developments in artificial intelligence and how these innovations are reshaping the marketing and business landscape. These sessions bring together practical case studies, emerging tools, and strategic frameworks tailored for businesses navigating an increasingly AI driven economy.\n\nThe most recent workshop, held at the Monash University Conference Centre, featured Lahiru Halkewella, Co-Founder and Chief Operating Officer of Enfection, alongside Shezri Junaid, Chief Strategy Officer. Together, they presented on \u201cThe New Marketing Operating System,\u201d a session focused on how the latest AI technologies are fundamentally transforming the way businesses plan, create, and execute their marketing efforts. The workshop sparked engaged discussion among attendees, many of whom were eager to explore how these tools could be applied within their own organisations.\n\n\u201cWe see Australia as a market that is ready to move beyond the hype surrounding AI and focus on practical application and measurable business outcomes. From SMEs and entrepreneurs to agencies and larger enterprises, our role is to help organisations bridge the gap between possibility and execution by translating emerging technologies into practical marketing solutions that drive growth, improve efficiency, and create meaningful customer experiences,\u201d said Lahiru Halkewela, Co-Founder of Enfection."
  },
