    "description": "The State wants our data, how will it protect it?",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/The-State-wants-our-data-how-will-it-protect-it/4-794125",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1783039186.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-07-03-dailyftlk-4dc6ef38-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e6e76efccdc9b1a0dab7055be54ff453",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1609,
    "chunk_text": "The State wants our data, how will it protect it?\n\nAlmost every week, headlines somewhere in the world report another major cyberattack. Governments, banks, hospitals, insurance companies and multinational corporations have all fallen victim to hackers, exposing millions of confidential records. Recent breaches involving government agencies and financial institutions have shown that no organisation is completely immune to cyber threats.\n\nThe recent ransomware attack on Sri Lanka's Pensions Department, which exposed hundreds of gigabytes of sensitive information due to outdated security measures, is a reminder that confidentiality depends not only on legal safeguards but also on strong cybersecurity, modern systems and effective supervision.\n\nCollecting information is only one part of the challenge. The systems that receive it must also be reliable. In practice, many have experienced online filing portals slowing down or even crashing when thousands of users attempt to upload information simultaneously. Such failures create frustration and sometimes leave users uncertain whether their submissions have been successfully received. If the State expects timely compliance, it must also provide the digital infrastructure and technical capacity needed to support it.\n\nCollecting information is relatively easy. Protecting it is far more difficult.\n\nThat reality makes Sri Lanka's recent introduction of Beneficial Ownership reporting an opportunity for a much broader discussion\u2014not about whether companies should disclose information, but about what happens after that information is collected."
  },
  {
